# Local git worktrees
.worktrees/

# Committed evidence. docs/results is the curated home for run products a reader
# is meant to check, so the blanket *.csv rule above must not silently drop them:
# a number in a table that nobody can trace back to a file is exactly the problem
# this directory exists to solve.
!docs/results/**/*.csv
!docs/INTEGRATION_COMMIT_DECISIONS_2026-09-01.csv

# Same rule, extended to the figure formats (T6). Without these the blanket *.png
# rule above dropped every rendered still while *.pdf -- which is not in that rule --
# was committed, so a publication figure set would have arrived half present with no
# sign that half was missing. Figures are evidence here for the same reason the CSVs
# are: a claim in a caption has to be traceable to the file that drew it.
!docs/results/**/*.png
!artifacts/publication/**/*.png
!artifacts/publication/**/*.pdf

# The animation is deliberately NOT excepted. closed_loop.gif is 3 MB, it carries no
# information the committed stills and replay.npz do not, and it is one command to
# regenerate:
#     python scripts/render_closed_loop.py docs/results/representative
